# Response headers for intheunionnow.com.
#
# Copied verbatim into `dist/` by Vite's publicDir, and read by Workers Static
# Assets (ADR-033). It is the app's ONLY source of security headers: Static
# Assets answers every file and every navigation itself, in
# single-page-application mode, and applies this file to all of them. The
# Worker script runs only for a miss that is not a navigation (a missing chunk,
# a crawler), and builds no document that runs script.
#
# `tools/check-observability.ts` requires the CSP here to allow Sentry's ingest
# origin; tools/smoke-production.sh asserts the CSP and HSTS actually reach the
# browser.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: on
  # connect-src MUST list Sentry's ingest origin or the browser blocks every
  # event before it leaves the page — a DSN alone is not enough, and that
  # failure is silent AND looks healthy (zero errors reported). `de`, not `us`:
  # this org is in Sentry's EU data region. Kept in lockstep with
  # SENTRY_INGEST_HOST in tools/check-observability.ts, which fails CI if this
  # drifts. Wildcarded subdomain because the host encodes the Sentry org id.
  #
  # The Convex entries fail the same silent way. The accounts client (ADR-030)
  # opens a WebSocket to the deployment for its reactive queries and POSTs
  # mutations over HTTPS, and `@convex-dev/auth` exchanges tokens against the
  # deployment's `.site` origin. Omit them and sign-in never completes, with no
  # error surface. Wildcarded per deployment name because production, a branch
  # deploy and a local `convex dev` differ. Both schemes are required — `wss:`
  # does NOT inherit from `https:`.
  #
  # script-src carries NO 'unsafe-inline': with it, an injected <script>
  # executes. The built `dist/index.html` contains zero inline scripts (Vite
  # bundles every module; the PWA registration is external). If a build ever
  # needs one, give that script a sha256 hash here, the way apps/srd does.
  # 'unsafe-inline' stays in style-src deliberately — Tailwind and React inline
  # styles need it, and style injection is not script execution.
  #
  # `https://storage.ko-fi.com` is the Ko-fi widget script (`KofiButton`).
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://storage.ko-fi.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.ingest.de.sentry.io https://*.convex.cloud wss://*.convex.cloud https://*.convex.site;

# Content-hashed bundle output from Vite's default assetsDir.
#
# Nothing else is marked immutable, and this is the one place this file
# deliberately differs from srd's. itun's `public/` holds `favicon.svg`,
# `icon-192.png`, `icon-512.png` and `logos/` — FIXED names that are mutated in
# place on redesign, so a year of `immutable` would mean a changed icon no
# amount of reloading can dislodge. They, and the shell, keep the platform's
# default `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`: a stale shell names chunks a
# deploy has rotated away.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
